# OpenClaw Security

## Critical: Never Commit Secrets

These files contain live credentials — NEVER include their values in code, comments, or commits:
- `openclaw.json` — channel tokens (Discord, Slack, Telegram), gateway token
- `.env` — API keys
- `agents/*/agent/auth-profiles.json` — provider API keys
- `identity/device-auth.json` — device credentials
- `exec-approvals.json` — socket token

`.gitignore` already excludes them. Verify before any `git add`.

## Secret Locations (read-only reference)
```
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY      → agents/main/agent/auth-profiles.json
GATEWAY_TOKEN          → openclaw.json → gateway.token
DISCORD_TOKEN          → openclaw.json → channels.discord.token
TELEGRAM_TOKEN         → openclaw.json → channels.telegram.token
```

## Safe Config Editing
1. Always backup before editing: `cp openclaw.json openclaw.json.bak`
2. Validate JSON after edit: `python3 -c "import json; json.load(open('openclaw.json'))"`
3. Never hardcode tokens in agent workspaces or markdown files

## Exec Safety
- Gateway deny list in `openclaw.json` blocks: camera, screen, contacts, location APIs
- Exec approvals stored in `exec-approvals.json` — do not manually bypass

## Channel Security
- Slack: allowlisted channel only — check `channels.slack.allowedChannels`
- Discord: token scoped to configured guilds only
